{
  "source": "What LibTmuxWorkspace.parse_config, validate and expand do with the keys and forms of tmuxp's workspace syntax. Each probe is expanded with home /home/u, base directory /workspace and the options given; packages/LibTmuxWorkspace/test/tmuxp_catalog.jl checks every entry against the loader, so the record changes when the loader does. The entry list and ids follow libtmux-ruby's record of the same syntax.",
  "statuses": {"supported": "Accepted and means what tmuxp means.", "difference": "Accepted, with the recorded difference.", "refused": "Refused with the recorded message."},
  "entries": [
    {"id":"session-name","scope":"session","key":"session_name","form":"string","status":"supported","probe":["session_name: a","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"]},
    {"id":"windows","scope":"session","key":"windows","form":"nonempty list of windows","status":"supported","probe":["session_name: a","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"]},
    {"id":"session-start-directory-absolute","scope":"session","key":"start_directory","form":"absolute path","status":"supported","probe":["session_name: a","start_directory: /var/log","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"]},
    {"id":"start-directory-relative","scope":"window","key":"start_directory","form":"relative path","status":"supported","probe":["session_name: a","start_directory: /var","windows:","  - window_name: w","    start_directory: log","    panes: [{}]"]},
    {"id":"start-directory-tilde","scope":"session","key":"start_directory","form":"leading ~","status":"difference","probe":["session_name: a","start_directory: ~/x","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"],"difference":"A leading ~ expands only to the home directory the caller passes to expand; without one, expansion raises an error. The loader reads no ambient environment.","observed":{"path":["session","start_directory"],"value":"/home/u/x"}},
    {"id":"variable-expansion-default","scope":"session","key":"${VAR}","form":"environment variable in a value","status":"difference","probe":["session_name: a","start_directory: ${HOME}/x","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"],"difference":"Left as written. tmuxp expands the variable from its own environment; the loader expands only the mapping passed to expand, so an unset name stays literal and the pane's shell expands it, if it expands anything.","observed":{"path":["session","start_directory"],"value":"/workspace/${HOME}/x"}},
    {"id":"variable-expansion-opt-in","scope":"session","key":"${VAR}","form":"environment variable in a value, with expand_environment","status":"difference","probe":["session_name: a","start_directory: ${HOME}/x","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"],"options":{"env":{"HOME":"/home/u"}},"difference":"Expanded from the mapping passed to expand, never from the process environment.","observed":{"path":["session","start_directory"],"value":"/home/u/x"}},
    {"id":"environment-strings","scope":"session","key":"environment","form":"mapping of strings","status":"supported","probe":["session_name: a","environment:","  A: b","windows:","  - window_name: w","    panes: [{}]"]},
